message: "If you use or reference this project, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "The Engineering Handbook: Open-Source Engineering Curricula (HLD + DSA + AI Engineering)"
abstract: >-
  An open-source umbrella for in-depth engineering curricula, hosting three
  sibling handbooks today and growing over time.
  The HLD Handbook (content/hld/) contains 159 teaching chapters across 12
  parts plus a 22-page trade-offs library (181 total pages, ~773,000 words,
  719 Mermaid diagrams, 3,100+ citations) covering everything from networking
  prerequisites to LLM serving architectures.
  The DSA Handbook (content/dsa/) contains 120 teaching chapters across 15
  parts, 37 pattern decision pages, 5 long-form LeetCode editorials, and 46
  interactive widget specs (~495,000 words, 226 Mermaid diagrams), with sibling
  Python / Java / C++ / Go solutions for 155 LeetCode problems.
  The AI Engineering Handbook (content/ai-eng/) contains 86 teaching chapters
  across 12 parts (~192,000 words, 87 figures, 750+ citations) on building
  and operating production AI products on top of foundation models.
  All books share the same CC BY-SA 4.0 license, contribution workflow, and
  CI quality bar.
